IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ppl-formulas`

-- Paid Parental Leave Act 2010, ss 41-44, 198(6) -- worked cases for ppl-formulas.l4.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were worked by hand from the
-- text and the sidecar formulas before running. The CPI index numbers are ILLUSTRATIVE, chosen to make the arithmetic plain:
-- December 2007 to December 2019 all 100, then 103 (2020), 103 (2021), 108.15 (2022), 108 (2023) and 111.24 (2024). They are not
-- the published numbers, so no limit here is the limit in force.

`illustrative December CPI` MEANS LIST 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 103, 103, 108.15, 108, 111.24

§ `s 43 -- the indexation factor`

-- 103 / 100 = 1.03. 111.24 / 108.15 = 1.02857: 1.028, the 4th place 5 (more than 4), so 1.029. A fall: 108 / 108.15, below 1, so 1.
#ASSERT `What is the PPL indexation factor` 103 100 EQUALS 1.03
#ASSERT `What is the PPL indexation factor` 111.24 108.15 EQUALS 1.029
#ASSERT `What is the PPL indexation factor` 108 108.15 EQUALS 1

-- $150,000 x 1.03 = $154,500. $162,225 x 1.029 = $166,929.525, to the nearest dollar $166,930.
#ASSERT `What is the PPL limit after one indexation` 150000 103 100 EQUALS 154500
#ASSERT `What is the PPL limit after one indexation` 162225 111.24 108.15 EQUALS 166930

§ `ss 41(1), 42-44 -- the individual limit on a day`

-- Before 1 July 2021: the $150,000 of s 41(1)(a).
#ASSERT `What is the individual PPL income limit from the CPI` 20210630 `illustrative December CPI` EQUALS JUST 150000
-- 1 July 2021: reference December 2020 (103), base the highest of December 2007-2019 (100): $154,500.
#ASSERT `What is the individual PPL income limit from the CPI` 20210701 `illustrative December CPI` EQUALS JUST 154500
-- 1 July 2022: 103 / 103 = 1, still $154,500; 1 July 2023: 108.15 / 103 = 1.05, $162,225; 1 July 2024: 108 against the highest
-- earlier, 108.15, so 1, still $162,225.
#ASSERT `What is the individual PPL income limit from the CPI` 20240801 `illustrative December CPI` EQUALS JUST 162225
-- 1 July 2025: 111.24 / 108.15 gives 1.029: $166,930, in force on 1 August 2025.
#ASSERT `What is the individual PPL income limit from the CPI` 20250801 `illustrative December CPI` EQUALS JUST 166930
-- 1 July 2026 needs December 2025, which the list does not have: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is the individual PPL income limit from the CPI` 20260701 `illustrative December CPI` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Before 1 October 2010 there was no limit.
#ASSERT `What is the individual PPL income limit from the CPI` 20100930 `illustrative December CPI` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 41(2), 42-44 -- the family limit on a day`

#ASSERT `What is the family PPL income limit from the CPI` 20231115 `illustrative December CPI` EQUALS JUST 350000
-- 1 July 2024: 108 / 108.15 is below 1, so 1: $350,000. 1 July 2025: 1.029, $360,150.
#ASSERT `What is the family PPL income limit from the CPI` 20241115 `illustrative December CPI` EQUALS JUST 350000
#ASSERT `What is the family PPL income limit from the CPI` 20250701 `illustrative December CPI` EQUALS JUST 360150
#ASSERT `What is the family PPL income limit from the CPI` 20230630 `illustrative December CPI` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 198(6) -- present value`

-- $1,200 a year at 10% for 5 years: ($1,200 / 0.1) x [1 - 1 / 1.1^5] = $4,548.94.
#ASSERT FLOOR (`What is the present value of my unpaid PPL debt` 1200 0.1 5) EQUALS 4548
